{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790347799,"nonce":"TSjfXylcni5TeJPQED9pgHU5hYE=","title":"Lua: repeat-until closes the body's \u003cclose\u003e variables before the condition runs","message":"Manual 3.3.4: the inner block of repeat-until ends after the condition, so a \u003cclose\u003e variable of the body is closed after the until expression is evaluated. zylua closes it at the body's end, before the condition. Reproducer: local i=0 repeat local x \u003cclose\u003e = setmetatable({}, {__close=function() print('close', i) end}); i=i+1 until (print('cond', i) or i\u003e=2) -- lua5.4: cond 1, close 1, cond 2, close 2; zylua (main 0f0e5585 and a900deba): close 1, cond 1, close 2, cond 2. Found while working on LO-tbc-generic-for; the fix is in the Stmt::Repeat lowering in crates/zyntax_lua/src/lower.rs (the body block closes before the condition is lowered).","files":null}]}